elcome. Please bring a white and colored shirt. Free parking available as well.\n\nThis event is free to attend. Arguments or fighting will not be tolerated and you will be asked to leave if you initiate any. Please RSVP and make sure you are on the \"going\" list in order to attend.","startDate":"2026-10-11T12:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hawthorne Valley Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"159 Ceremonial Dr, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Soccer Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-soccer-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Soccer Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Riverdale Park 5K Run / Walk / Jog","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/events/316649784/","description":"5K every week till the snows come down! Or try to!\n\nWe'll meet by the track. I'll be there early to warm up. We will start the 5K exactly at 9:30am. As mentioned in the About Us,\n\n* Using the park track we can all go at our own pace and never really be left behind unless we all finish way ahead of you. :D I think an hour is enough time to dedicate to the run. I'm pretty slow, so you will likely have me around for most of the hour.\n* Members are free to leave the run whenever they want.\n* Bring your kids, your pets, your partners, etc.\n* All encouraged to stick around afterwards and enjoy the park or neighbourhood on your own.\n* Let's get stronger, healthier and foster a great community at the same time.\n\nWe also welcome runners who are not in our neighbourhood and want to join us spiritually and run from their own neighbourhoods. :-) Imagine how much healthier and communal the world would be if we all stopped for an hour once in a while to run together; re-centring and re-charging together?","startDate":"2026-10-11T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"RIVERDALE PARK","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1 Millbrook Crescent, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Riverdale Park 5K","url":"https://www.meetup.com/riverdale-5k/"},"performer":"Riverdale Park 5K"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sunday Worship Service","url":"https://www.meetup.com/st-tims-wellness/events/316650207/","description":"Please join us for a traditional worship service every Sunday, with music from our wonderful choir and organist. Communion (the Lord’s Supper) is a part of every Sunday service. Join us for coffee hour after the service for conversation and a snack","startDate":"2026-10-11T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"100 Old Orchard Grove","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Old Orchard Grove, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Church of St Timothy Wellness","url":"https://www.meetup.com/st-tims-wellness/"},"performer":"Church of St Timothy Wellness"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"OutDoor Recreation Soccer (CANCELLED)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto_asians/events/316650307/","description":"Smaller group on a small field, recreational, low level, only very small group. It's a smaller field, usually, we play 4 on 4 or max 5 on 5. No subs.\n\nOutdoor turf and free soccer event, . The event is none competitive soccer for low levels only, the game should be easy and fun, so we can get little bit sweat while enjoy the weather. This is no contact soccer,\n\nWe should have have another what's app group of friends joining us on the soccer field, all you need to bring is good spirit and your own water.\n\nshould be lots parking around the school and it's few mins walk from the subway station, once you get there, we will be gathered on the field. If we cancel the event, I will post on the event board here.\n\nIf the game is cancelled, I will post on the comment board.\n\nThis event is sponsored by Harbord Bakery (http://www.harbordbakery.ca/), Bakery on Mavis(http://www.bakeryonmavis.ca/) Brazil Bakery (http://brazilbakerypastry.ca/) Kensington Natural Bakery (http://kensingtonnaturalbakery.ca/) and EJoyCity.ca (https://www.ejoycity.ca/), iBake (http://i-bake.ca/), La Novita Bakery(http://lanovitabakery.ca) Absolute Bakery(http://absolutecafe.ca) they will give 10% off on everything. Simply, just tell them you are here for the meetup event.","startDate":"2026-10-11T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"McKee Public School","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"35 Church Ave, North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Asian Business & Social Network (3,000 friends, #1 @ Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto_asians/"},"performer":"Asian Business & Social Network (3,000 friends, #1 @ Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Wilket Creek, Serena Grundy, Sunnybrook, Edwards Garden AND Stretching!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/events/316635938/","description":"**MeetUp Point: James for Entrance is off Leslie Street. Turn left on Leslie to Parking Lot 2 in Wilkett Creek Park**\n(Don't follow the pin!)\n\n**Join James for a 12 km hike that is challenging!**\n\nStarting past Wilcott Parking Lot 2, we will be passing through a number of parks and hills.\nFor lunch we can stop at the TBG Bloom cafe for lunch or coffee ---- you might need one; or bring your own lunch.\nWe will finish the hike with much needed yoga streches.\nIt might be muddy, so ensure you have proper footwear!\nAlso layers please, as we are heading into cooler weather!","startDate":"2026-10-11T14:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Wilket Creek Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1120 Leslie St, North York, ON M3C, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"These Boots Are Made for Hiking","url":"https://www.meetup.com/these-boots-are-made-for-hiking/"},"performer":"These Boots Are Made for Hiking"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/events/316723632/","description":"# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂\n\n### A Hidden Ravine, Easy Walking & Great Conversation\n\nSometimes the best parts of Toronto are the ones most people drive right past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed fall walk along the **Gus Harris Trail**, a quiet ravine trail that follows **Taylor-Massey Creek** through Scarborough and East York.\n\nThis isn't a challenging hike. It's an easy, mostly flat walk through one of Toronto's quieter green spaces, with plenty of time to enjoy the changing leaves, get some fresh air, and meet other people along the way.\n\nWe'll follow the creek, walk beneath the trees, and take our time enjoying the fall scenery.\nThe goal isn't to race to the end of the trail. **It's to get outside, have some good conversations, and enjoy the company.**\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:** Taylor-Massey Creek takes its name from two prominent Toronto families. The Taylor family was associated with the Don Valley Brick Works, now home to Evergreen Brick Works.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about **two hours** walking along the trail, taking our time, chatting, and getting to know one another.\nThis is a **social walk, not a race.**\n\nThe route has very few hills, making it a comfortable walk for most people with a reasonable level of fitness.\nWe'll finish back where we started.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typical Toronto fall weather.\nPlease dress appropriately for the conditions and wear comfortable walking shoes. The trail may be damp or muddy depending on recent weather.\nBring water and a snack, and dress in layers if the temperature is changing throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station, by Victoria Park Road.\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Victoria Park Subway Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n🦟 Bug spray if needed\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who enjoys fall scenery 🍂\n* People looking for an easy trail\n* Anyone who wants to get outside and get moving\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto's hidden green spaces\n* Anyone looking for a relaxed social outing\n* People who want to meet new people and make friends\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Victoria Park Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Scarborough, ON M4C 5L9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Try New Things in Toronto!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/"},"performer":"Try New Things in Toronto!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231805/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Historic Mount Pleasant Cemetery - Fall Colours","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693091/","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe only authorized cemeteries within York were Anglican or Roman Catholic. Citizens who did not belong to either church had no choice but to find burial arrangements outside York.\n\nThe General Burying Ground received Royal Assent in 1826 and land that came to be known as Potters Field was acquired and started operation soon afterwards. Over time, additional cemetery lands were added and in 1873, a new cemetery available to all citizens was established. The new cemetery was situated on the farm land of the Cawthra family near Yonge Street.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. Please dress for the weather. This walk will begin and end outside the Yorkminster Park Baptist Church at 1585 Yonge Street just north of Heath Street.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person! This tour has space for **11** explorers, so if you do plan on attending please secure your tickets early.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Yorkminster Park Baptist Church","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1585 Yonge St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sunday Noontime Tennis - York University Heights TENNIS AND TUNES 🔊🎵🎶 📻 ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/greater-toronto-ontario-area-tennis-players/events/316651705/","description"